Between June and August 2026, a coordinated wave of cyber attacks targeted European public administration, energy grids, and digital supply chains. These retaliatory attacks on EU infrastructure have exposed severe, shared single points of failure across the institutional supply chain, posing immediate intraday liquidity and DORA compliance risks to the Group's balance sheet.
